   "text": "http : / / globalnews . ca / news / 842183 / australian - english - climbers - fall - to - their - deaths - in - new - zealand - mountains / September 15 , 2013 11 : 26 pm Australian , English climbers <1 fall> to their <2 deaths> in New Zealand mountains One Australian and one English climber have <3 fallen> to their <4 deaths> in New Zealand . Police Inspector Dave Gaskin said Monday the two incidents on consecutive days in the Aoraki - Mt . Cook National Park were not related and were not due to bad weather . He says they come as a reminder that climbers need to use extreme caution . On Friday , 36 - year - old Duncan Raite <5 died> after <6 slipping> and <7 falling> about 60 metres ( 200 feet ) from a ridge . The New Zealand - born Australian was planning to do some ski touring . He ’ d been dropped off by helicopter and was walking to a hut when he fell . On Saturday , 32 - year - old Englishman Robert Buckley <8 fell> about 600 metres ( 2 , 000 feet ) while <9 climbing> to a small hut on Mount Sefton . Gaskin said Buckley was wearing crampons but was inexperienced .",
